        "id": 3678645
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-16T22:20:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Wan-Teh for looking into this.\n\nAfter digging a bit further, what the TODO describes is actually inaccurate -- mode 1 isn\u0027t failing because the clip is low resolution, but because `screendata.y4m` mostly contains anti-aliased text, and so mode 1 is unable to classify those regions as candidates to use palette mode and intraBC.\n\nIn other words, it\u0027s \"by design\" that mode 1 (as currently designed) fails to turn `screen_content` on for `screendata.y4m`.\n\nTherefore, I\u0027ll modify the comment so it reads like this instead:\n```c\n  // The test below is only enabled for mode 2 because the input consists of\n  // anti-aliased text, which mode 1 can\u0027t determine as screen content \n```",
      "parentUuid": "af84eb1d_9f1a3a3d",
      "revId": "e2986c456fc1ca059dd3f7e20472f327213b942e",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    }
